{
  "_doc": "THE DECK. One entry per page — this is the part a human writes. Nothing here is in seconds: atBar is a BAR NUMBER on the measured grid (data/features.json), and every entrance is measured in BEATS from the page turn. A page turn is a cut on the grid; that is what makes a slide deck that is also frame-accurate to the song. Blocks are drawn in order inside their slot; give a block `at` (beats) to time it by hand, or leave it out and the page shares `enterBeats` evenly between them. Mark ONE block per page `hit: true` — the moment the page is about; the lens reacts to it (bloom, rays, aberration). `theme` names one of config.json -> palettes. The last page demonstrates MV mode: layout \"stage\" with a full-bleed \"scene\" motif and a \"lyric\" line over it. A `figure` is optional and ORTHOGONAL to the motif: the same place with her somewhere else in it doing something else is a different shot, which is how a film gets 85 shots out of 30 places. pose: walk|stand|sit|kneel|reach|lookup|crouch; facing 0 = seen from behind. `also` + ghost:true draws the one she remembers.\n\nThe MV page carries a subtitle on EVERY shot, and the subtitle box is COMPUTED, not chosen by hand: `dx`/`w` on the `lyric` block are fractions of the `head` slot (x 0.06, w 0.88) and come from captionBox() in tools/shotlist.example.mjs — the line goes on whichever side leaves more room, measured from her x, her pose's half width (a seated body is 1.8x wider than `s` suggests) and which side the ghost stands on. Never leave a shot wordless: where nothing is sung, write the song's own syllables or hold the last line. See references/subtitles.md.",
